{
  "A document manager that arranges content the way code editors arrange files: documents in tabs, tabs in groups, and groups split side by side or one above the other. A document's content can be any component, such as a form, a grid or plain text, and it is moved rather than recreated when its tab goes to another group. Every user action is also a method, with a cancelable event before it and a notification after it, and the whole layout can be saved to JSON and restored. Preview and pinned tabs, sizes and copies are covered in [Tabs](/tabdocs/tabs), and context menus, lists and keyboard shortcuts in [Menus and keys](/tabdocs/menus).": "",
  "Documents, groups and splits": "",
  "Create a manager, give it a size, and call `open` to add documents. `split` opens a new group beside an existing one. To resize groups, drag the line between them, or focus it and use the arrow keys. Double-click the line to make the sizes equal, or double-click a tab to give its group all the available space. The buttons at the end of each tab strip split and maximize the group.": "",
  "Every behavior is a prop that accepts a value or a tracked function, and a document's own `closable` and `contentLifetime` take precedence over the manager's. In this example, Alpha cannot be closed and Gamma has unsaved changes.": "",
  "Every user action is also a method (`open`, `close`, `activate`, `split`, `move`, `closeGroup`, `focusGroup`, `maximizeGroup`, `restoreGroups`, `evenSizes`, `resizeGroup`). Each one raises a cancelable `on…ing` event first and an `on…ed` event afterward, and `byUser` indicates which of the two started it.": "",
  "Unsaved changes": "",
  "`dirty` tracks a function of the form's data, and the tab shows a dot in place of its close button. `onClosing` sets `e.promise` to prompt the user, and the document closes when the promise resolves to `true`.": "",
  "Saving and restoring the layout": "",
  "`saveLayout()` writes plain JSON containing the tree of splits with each child's share, the groups with their documents (`id`, `type`, `title`, `state`, `pinned`, `preview`), the active and recently used tabs, and the active and maximized groups. `loadLayout(json, factory)` rebuilds it, and the factory creates each document by its `type`.": "",
  "Content lifetime": "",
  "`contentLifetime` determines when a document's content is created and how long it lives. Whatever the setting, moving a tab or splitting a group never recreates the content, because the same component moves with it.": "",
  "Lifetime": "",
  "Created when the document opens, and kept with its state until the document closes.": "",
  "Created the first time it is shown, and then kept.": "",
  "Created when shown and disposed when hidden. It is created again from `content` (or the manager's `factory`) the next time, with the document's `state`. A component provided directly cannot be recreated, so it is kept.": "",
  "The keys work while focus is inside the manager. Each one is a list of key combinations in `keys`, so any of them can be changed or disabled. A browser tab reserves Ctrl+W, Ctrl+Tab, Ctrl+Page Up/Down and often Ctrl+1…9, so the default keys are ones a browser lets through. The key in brackets also works where the browser allows it, and an installed app uses the desktop preset (`keyPreset`). The recently used list, back and forward, reopening and the remaining keys are covered in [Menus and keys](/tabdocs/menus#keyboard).": "",
  "Moves to the next or previous tab of the active group, wrapping around at the ends (`nextTab`, `previousTab`).": "",
  "Sets focus on group 1 to 9 (`focusGroup`, written as `Ctrl+Alt+{n}`).": "",
  "Splits the active group to the right. The active document moves to the new group if it is not the only one, otherwise a copy opens there (`splitRight`).": "",
  "Moves to the next, previous, first or last tab, which also activates it unless `activation` is manual (`stripNext`, `stripPrevious`, `stripFirst`, `stripLast`).": "",
  "Activates the tab.": "",
  "Closes the tab (`closeFocusedTab`).": "",
  "Makes the group before the splitter smaller or larger by `resizeStep`, or as small or as large as possible (`resizeSmaller`, `resizeLarger`, `resizeMin`, `resizeMax`).": "",
  "Moves from the tab strip (one Tab stop, on the active tab) to the group buttons, the content, the splitter and the next group.": "",
  "Each group is a `group` named “Group 1”, “Group 2” and so on. With `label`, the manager is a `region`.": "",
  "One `tablist` per group (“Documents in group 1”) of `tab` elements, each controlling its `tabpanel`. A roving `tabindex` keeps one Tab stop per strip. A tab announces “unsaved changes” while its document is dirty, and `aria-keyshortcuts` names the key that closes it.": "",
  "`separator` elements with `aria-orientation`, `aria-valuenow` (the share of the group before it, from 0 to 100) and `aria-controls`.": "",
  "A polite live region announces what was opened, closed, moved, split, maximized or restored (`announce`).": "",
  "A group remembers where focus was inside it, and closing the focused tab moves focus to the tab that takes its place.": "",
  "All text comes from `uiLocale.strings` (`tabDocs…`: group and strip names, “No open documents”, “unsaved changes”, buttons and announcements), in English and Turkish. `texts` overrides some for one manager.": "",
  "The root. It has `data-maximized` while a group is maximized and `data-resizing` while a splitter is being dragged, plus `data-tab-size`, `data-pinned-size`, `data-pinned-row`, `data-wrap` and `data-scroll-buttons` from the props.": "",
  "A split, with `data-orientation`.": "",
  "A splitter (`role=\"separator\"`).": "",
  "A group, with `data-active`, `data-empty`, `data-maximized` and `data-locked`.": "",
  "The strip row, the tab list with its scroll buttons, the `tablist` with its pinned row and the row of other tabs, and the kit Toolbar with the group buttons.": "",
  "A tab, with `aria-selected`, `data-dirty`, `data-close` (`always`, `active`), `data-pinned`, `data-preview`, `data-tone` and `data-icon`.": "",
  "The parts of a tab. A badge displayed as a dot has `data-dot`.": "",
  "The \"…\" and recently used lists.": "",
  "The content area, a document's `tabpanel`, and the text of an empty group.": "",
  "Units: the area behind the groups, a group, its strip and the line under it, the pinned tabs row, a panel, and the text of an empty group.": "",
  "Units: a tab (`hover`, `selected`, `before-selected`, `focus`, `dragging`, `title` …, whose end side is the line between tabs), the bar on it (`selected`, and `active` in the active group), and its parts in each tone.": "",
  "Units: the scroll buttons, the thin scrollbar, the count on \"…\", and a splitter and its line (`across`, `active`).": "",
  "Sizes used by the layout (a shrinking tab keeps its icon, its close button and a few letters).": "",
  "The position of the bar on a tab.": "",
  "The focus ring's space at the ends of a small toolbar, and the sizes for touch.": "",
  "Names the manager, making it a `region` landmark. This is the same property as `text`.": "",
  "Which tabs show a close button: every tab, the active tab and the tab under the pointer, or none. A document with `closable: false` shows none.": "",
  "When content is created and how long it lives (see below). A document's own value takes precedence.": "",
  "Closes a group when it has no documents left. The last group never closes.": "",
  "Where `open` places a tab when no `index` is given.": "",
  "Which tab becomes active when the active tab closes: the most recently used tab, or a neighbor.": "",
  "With `auto`, the arrow keys activate the tab they reach. With `manual`, Enter or Space activates it.": "",
  "The minimum size of a group, in pixels. A splitter stops there.": "",
  "How far a splitter key moves a splitter, in pixels.": "",
  "The split, maximize and \"…\" buttons at the end of each strip.": "",
  "Double-clicking a tab maximizes its group or restores the groups. On a preview tab, it keeps the tab open instead.": "",
  "The default keys: keys a browser tab lets through, or those of a desktop editor. `auto` uses the desktop keys in an installed app.": "",
  "Changes specific keys, and the others keep the preset's values. An empty list disables a key.": "",
  "Creates the content of a document that does not provide its own, usually by its `type`.": "",
  "Strings for this manager only, which override `uiLocale.strings`.": "",
  "Announces opened, closed, moved, split and maximized states to screen readers.": "",
  "Stays the same for the life of the document, and is generated when omitted. `findDocument(id)` finds a document by it.": "",
  "The key used to restore a layout. The `loadLayout` factory and the manager's `factory` read it.": "",
  "The tab's text. The description follows it in a lighter style, and distinguishes documents with the same title.": "",
  "An icon before the title, and a short text or count after it.": "",
  "Shown when the pointer rests on the tab or the tab has focus. By default, it is the title and the description.": "",
  "Marks unsaved changes. A dot replaces the close button, which returns under the pointer, and screen readers announce “unsaved changes”.": "",
  "The default is `true`. With `false`, there is no close button and the user cannot close the document, although code still can.": "",
  "A pinned tab stays at the start, and a preview tab is replaced by the next preview. Both are saved with the layout. See [Tabs](/tabdocs/tabs).": "",
  "A count or a dot, a color, toolbar buttons while active, and the content of a copy. See [Tabs](/tabdocs/tabs) and [Menus and keys](/tabdocs/menus).": "",
  "This document's own lifetime. `undefined` uses the manager's setting.": "",
  "The content: a component, or a function that creates it (and creates it again after `dispose`).": "",
  "Application data for the document, saved with the layout.": "",
  "Where it is open, and the content created for it.": "",
  "The same as the manager's methods.": "",
  "The groups in layout order: left to right, top to bottom.": "",
  "Every open document, group by group.": "",
  "The group that has or last had focus, and its active document.": "",
  "The maximized group, or `null` when none is maximized.": "",
  "The most recently used documents, those `reopenClosed` can open, and the history. See [Menus and keys](/tabdocs/menus).": "",
  "static": "",
  "The two key presets.": "",
  "In strip order, the active document, and the most recently used first.": "",
  "Its position in `groups`, starting from 0, and its state.": "",
  "A locked group does not receive documents opened without naming the group. `lock()` and `unlock()` raise their events and are announced.": "",
  "The document of the group's preview tab, if it has one.": "",
  "The manager's methods for this group.": "",
  "Opens a `TabDocument`, or one created from options, in a group (the active group by default). An already open document is activated. Returns `null` when `onOpening` cancels.": "",
  "Closes the document as the close button does. Returns `false` when `onClosing` keeps it open.": "",
  "Closes the documents of a group, or of all groups. Returns `false` when some remain open.": "",
  "Makes it the active tab of its group, and that group the active group. `focus` moves focus into the content.": "",
  "Moves to the next or previous tab, wrapping around at the ends (Ctrl + Page Down/Up).": "",
  "Moves it to another position in its group, or to another group. The content moves with it unchanged.": "",
  "Adds a new group on the `'left'`, `'right'`, `'up'` or `'down'` side, and `doc` moves into it. With a `group` of `null`, the new group runs along that edge of the whole layout.": "",
  "Closes the group's documents, and then the group. The last group stays, empty.": "",
  "Makes it active and sets focus on what last had focus in it.": "",
  "Gives one group all the space. The other groups stay hidden, unchanged.": "",
  "Makes every group of every split the same size.": "",
  "Sets a group's size along its split, in pixels or as a share (`'30%'`). The next group gives up or takes the difference.": "",
  "The layout as plain JSON (see below).": "",
  "Replaces the current layout with a saved one, closing the current documents without prompting. `factory(saved)` returns the document, its options or its content.": "",
  "`{ document, group, index, active, byUser }`. `opening` is cancelable and can change `group` and `index`.": "",
  "`{ document, group, index, byUser }`. `closing` is cancelable, or can set `e.promise` (`Promise<boolean>`) to prompt first.": "",
  "`{ document, previous, group, byUser }`. `activating` (a tab is being selected) is cancelable, and `activated` also runs when another group becomes active.": "",
  "`{ document, from, fromIndex, to, toIndex, byUser }`. `moving` is cancelable.": "",
  "`{ group, direction, document, byUser }`, plus `newGroup` afterward. `splitting` is cancelable. `group` is `null` when the new group runs along an edge of the whole layout.": "",
  "`{ change, group, byUser }`, where `change` is `'split'`, `'closeGroup'`, `'resize'`, `'evenSizes'`, `'maximize'`, `'restore'`, `'move'` (a whole group moved or merged) or `'load'`. `changing` is cancelable (a split uses `onSplitting`).": ""
